  "caption": "Quinn started night shifts and everything ached a bit more. Sound familiar?\n\nShort or broken sleep can lower pain tolerance and slow recovery, so aches can feel louder on a night roster.\n\nA few things that often help: protect your day sleep (dark, quiet, cool room), have caffeine early in the shift, keep short regular strength sessions, and move a little every hour on long shifts.\n\nIf pain hangs around or starts affecting your sleep or work, it's worth getting it looked at early. If sleepiness is affecting your driving, or sleep is a constant struggle, chat with your GP.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
